sumdb: ignore unrelated hashes in Lookup

A malicious sumdb server could return a validly signed record for an
unrelated module containing an extra hash line in the tree head's
extension area. Client.Lookup validated only a portion of the returned
record (via tlog.ParseRecord) but then searched for matching lines
across the full, unvalidated record text, allowing an attacker-supplied
hash to slip through unverified. The fix caches only the hash lines
returned by tlog.ParseRecord (the validated set) instead of the raw
record data, so lookups can no longer match unauthenticated lines.

Fixes CVE-2026-56864 (golang/go#80745).

